{"beat": 3, "name": "THE CRACK", "text": "Take one product off the demo catalog. TH-OVEMIT-22, from Tarnhollow, demo data, about $3.5M a year across 24 products. This one has 12 months of history where the price moved and the units moved with it. That's far more than a few weeks. Fit the demand curve through it and you get a best guess: an elasticity of -2.20. Units fall faster than price rises, by about that ratio. Now ask the fit how sure it is. The honest range runs from -3.52 to -0.88. At one end a price rise is a disaster. At the other it's nearly free. Same product, same data, same fit. The width of that range is 2.64, and it's the thing your test never showed you.", "provider": "library", "words": [{"word": "Take", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.302}, {"word": "one", "start": 0.36, "end": 0.511}, {"word": "product", "start": 0.557, "end": 0.882}, {"word": "off", "start": 0.917, "end": 1.01}, {"word": "the", "start": 1.045, "end": 1.115}, {"word": "demo", "start": 1.138, "end": 1.347}, {"word": "catalog.", "start": 1.393, "end": 2.009}, {"word": "TH-OVEMIT-22,", "start": 2.392, "end": 4.261}, {"word": "from", "start": 4.307, "end": 4.47}, {"word": "Tarnhollow,", "start": 4.528, "end": 5.283}, {"word": "demo", "start": 5.666, "end": 5.909}, {"word": "data,", "start": 5.968, "end": 6.409}, {"word": "about", "start": 6.502, "end": 6.792}, {"word": "$3.5M", "start": 6.861, "end": 7.674}, {"word": "a", "start": 7.79, "end": 7.999}, {"word": "year", "start": 8.081, "end": 8.348}, {"word": "across", "start": 8.557, "end": 8.975}, {"word": "24", "start": 9.056, "end": 9.404}, {"word": "products.", "start": 9.451, "end": 10.066}, {"word": "This", "start": 10.391, "end": 10.577}, {"word": "one", "start": 10.646, "end": 10.774}, {"word": "has", "start": 10.809, "end": 10.925}, {"word": "12", "start": 10.995, "end": 11.215}, {"word": "months", "start": 11.273, "end": 11.459}, {"word": "of", "start": 11.482, "end": 11.529}, {"word": "history", "start": 11.598, "end": 11.935}, {"wo